--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled binaries
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The macOS application bundle carries three executables whose source is not this
repository. Each one runs as its own process. None of them is loaded into a
Tortie process.

  ripgrep, through @vscode/ripgrep     Andrew Gallant, MIT or Unlicense
  specstory                            SpecStory, bundled under a pinned release
  tmux                                 Nicholas Marriott and contributors, ISC

The tmux copy is built from source at packaging time by build/build-tmux.mjs,
from the three tarballs pinned in build/tmux-release.json. libevent and utf8proc
are linked into it as static archives, so no library of theirs is installed or
shipped as a separate file. ncurses comes from the operating system and is not
bundled.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
tmux
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Tortie bundles tmux 3.7b and runs it as a separate process on a private socket.
It never reads the user's own tmux configuration and never touches their default
server.

